The measurement runs (results/runB_*.tsv, results/trig_g12.txt) used a temporary environment knob
that is NOT in the committed code. Modes: off = no restarts (the code before this change),
trigger = `_q2_boundary_restarts` with the usual trigger only (`force = false`),
force = `force = true` (the committed rule, which applies it to every fit whose SD formulas
contain a covariate; all measured cells are such fits). Equivalent patch to
`_fit_binomial_sd_regression` (src/binomial_sd_regression.jl):

    _mode = get(ENV, "DRM_BINOM_INDEP_MODE", "trigger")        # off | trigger | force
    if !correlated && q >= 2 && _mode != "off"
        res = _q2_boundary_restarts(...; force = _mode == "force")   # otherwise as committed
